 "study": "docs/research/MEMORY_LOADING.md",
 "increment": "ml-l13",
 "previous": "ml-l12",
 "phase": "L13 (loading time): the loading packages read ahead during the menu; the startup package read once",
 "change": "The first loading step re-read the startup package (already read by start()) and then read five packages (catalog, loading, interface, menu with War, arena) one after another while the game thread waited. The session now keeps start()'s startup package and, right after the started event, starts OriginalConcurrentInputs.Background, a thread that reads the five packages as OriginalRuntimeLoadingPackages (each a Result); the first loading step waits for it and takes the values in bundled's order, so the first failing package in that order throws its own error at the same point. The loaded event reports packagesWaitSeconds. On Android the read-ahead thread is allowed every core at nice 10 (its package threads inherit the nice value). Package loads only read, verify and decode.",
 "profile": "A12 ml-l12-loadprof game-thread timeline: seconds 1-4.5 the menu builds bitmaps with all load threads idle; seconds 5-9 the game thread waits on the packages (4 s of the 15 s load) after re-reading the startup package",
 "variants": "Phone probes before the gate (l13-probe-phone, l13b-probe-phone; runs in probe-runs below): A (every core, nice 10) load 10.55-10.97 s, wait 0.15-0.38 s, menu 4.6-4.8 s, start to loaded 17.1-17.5 s; B (slow cluster only, 4 threads, nice 10) load 12.92-13.22 s, wait 2.45-2.64 s, menu 4.0-4.1 s, start to loaded 18.6-19.0 s; L12 load 14.98 s, menu 3.8 s, start to loaded 20.5 s. A kept.",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no correctness bug (error order and points unchanged, no race with main-thread state, Background's handoff sound, Swift 5 isolation correct, Android setpriority per thread and inherited); risks recorded: a trap or out-of-memory during a package read now happens during the menu; while the game thread waits the read-ahead runs at nice 10 (could wait longer if other processes compete); the read-ahead result stays alive if the session stops before loading (follow-up: clear it in stop()); comment nit",
 "notes": "The menu phase before loading is ~0.8 s longer (4.5-4.7 s against 3.6-3.9 s) while the read-ahead competes with the game thread; start to loaded is still 3.5 s shorter. Two phone runs re-extracted the assets after their install (25 s startups, S1).",
